      ],
      "text": "Closest rival: validate N3 and use routine bulk at tick 0. Compare boundary ledgers through 4. Individual delivery predicts a new N2 recognition at tick 1; bulk predicts a duplicate N1 delivery first. Both predict the same N1 display mismatch through boundary 3. This feasible probe separates queue consequences, not rival causes of the exact anomaly; these are model predictions, not observed trial results."
    },
    {
      "id": "residue_defeat",
      "source_refs": [
        "O5",
        "C4",
        "C6",
        "P1",
        "P2",
        "R8"
      ],
      "text": "No admissible separating ablation is available. Interrupting the declared registration-to-request eligibility connection prevents P2 requests; disabling registration sacrifices P1. Switching bulk to individual retains eligibility. Changing the fixed display delay requires unavailable configuration access. Parent loss or an unchanged, equally explained mismatch defeats this recipe."
    },
    {
      "id": "residue_burden",
      "source_refs": [
        "C1",
        "C3",
        "R1",
        "R2",
        "R5",
        "R6"
      ],
      "text": "The diagnostic spends one registration-clerk tick and one of six dispatcher actions. Server deliveries still consume one slot each; duplicates reduce remaining recognition capacity. Ledger reading adds no clerk labor. This diagnostic alone does not establish full-window success."
    },
    {
      "id": "residue_unknowns",
      "source_refs": [
